"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and an initial phase one budget of $500,000. The project team was expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, which was ahead of schedule. A breakthrough in predictive analytics has been achieved in phase two, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget has been increased to $55,000, and security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year. Celebrations for the testing milestone are planned for October 10th."
